#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""needs-you-linear: turn your Linear inbox (assignments, comments, mentions, status changes) into needs-you cards.

  needs-you-linear [--dry-run] [--verbose] [--state PATH]

Opt-in: it does nothing until a Linear personal API key is configured. Run it every ~5
minutes (cron, a systemd user timer or a LaunchAgent) on one machine. Each run makes one
GraphQL request to https://api.linear.app/graphql (more only when the inbox has more than a
page of new notifications):

  1. The notifications updated since the last run (assignments, comments and replies,
     mentions, status changes), and the ones behind the cards already open, so a read,
     archived or snoozed notification clears its card.
  2. viewer.assignedIssues (not done or canceled), so an issue that leaves it (done,
     canceled or unassigned from you) clears its card.
  3. One card per issue, key <context>:linear:<ISSUE-ID>, titled by the latest event, with a
     count line as its body. It is re-posted while it holds (so its --expires-in keeps
     moving), and resolved when every notification behind it is read, archived or snoozed,
     the issue is done, canceled or no longer yours, or after 24 h with nothing new.

The key is read from a file (mode 600, owned by you) and sent only to the API URL; it is
never logged, printed, stored in the state file or passed to another program. Everything
read from Linear is untrusted: only issue titles and status names (cleaned, redacted and
truncated) reach a card, and only https://linear.app links to that issue. Comment bodies are
never read. It always exits 0.

Config (environment, else ~/.config/needs-you/env):
  NEEDS_YOU_LINEAR_KEY_FILE   file holding the personal API key (default ~/.config/needs-you/linear-key
                              if it exists). Must be a regular file, yours, mode 600 or stricter
  NEEDS_YOU_LINEAR_KEY        the key itself, from the process environment only (not the env file)
  NEEDS_YOU_LINEAR_CATEGORIES events to post, comma list (default all): assigned status comment mention,
                              or Linear's names (assignments statusChanges commentsAndReplies mentions);
                              "-mention" turns one off
  NEEDS_YOU_LINEAR_STATUSES   priority by the issue's status: "Blocked=urgent,In Review=normal,*=low";
                              "Backlog=off" posts no status-change card for that status
  NEEDS_YOU_LINEAR_TEAMS      team key=context:priority, "ACME=work:normal,OPS=work:urgent". When set,
                              also the list of teams to watch (default: every team, default context)
  NEEDS_YOU_LINEAR_INTERVAL   minutes between runs (default 5); cards expire after 3x this
  NEEDS_YOU_LINEAR_MAX_CARDS  at most this many cards open at once (default 20; urgent first)
  NEEDS_YOU_LINEAR_MAX_AGE_H  a card with nothing new for this many hours resolves (default 24)
  NEEDS_YOU_LINEAR_API        the GraphQL URL (default https://api.linear.app/graphql; https, or http
                              to a loopback address for tests)
  NEEDS_YOU_BIN               path to the needs-you CLI (default: on PATH, else ~/.local/bin)

Priority is the highest of the status rule, the team's base and the event's floor (comment
and mention: normal; assigned and status: low).

State: ~/.local/state/needs-you/linear.json (mode 600): what it posted, the notifications
behind open cards, the time of the last run. No key.
Python 3.9+ standard library only.
"""
